Poor&#146;s credit rating of BBB-, which is the lowest
investment grade rating given by Standard&nbsp;&#38;
Poor&#146;s, is assigned to companies or issuances that exhibit
adequate protection parameters. However, adverse economic
conditions or changing circumstances are more likely to lead to
a weakened capacity of the company to meet its financial
commitments. A Standard&nbsp;&#38; Poor&#146;s credit rating of
AAA+, which is the highest investment grade rating given by
Standard&nbsp;&#38; Poor&#146;s, is assigned to companies or
issuances with extremely strong capacities to meet their
financial commitments. Thus, investment grade tenants will be
judged by Standard&nbsp;&#38; Poor&#146;s to have at least
adequate protection parameters, and will in some cases have
extremely strong financial positions.
